+Whether a thread answers questions from linked machines is set at three levels,
+and the nearest one that is set wins:
+
+1. The thread: **Answer linked questions** in its thread menu.
+2. Its project: **Answer linked questions** in **Settings → Projects**, or in the
+   project folder's menu in the sidebar. It applies to every thread of the
+   project that has no choice of its own.
+3. The machine: **Answer linked questions in every thread** in **Settings →
+   Environments → Linked environments** (the **List** view). It is off by
+   default.
+
+The thread and project menus offer **Default**, **On** and **Off**; **Default**
+names what the thread or project follows right now, for example
+**Default (off, from this machine)**. Choose it to return to that. Only a session
+that manages access can change any level; agents, links and scheduled tasks
+cannot, and no file in a project folder can switch it on. Question threads,
+subagents, side chats and a workflow's agent steps never answer. A thread set to
+**Off** is not listed and cannot be asked, and its messages are never read for an
+answer, also not through a fork. A fork of it, or a thread its agent starts on
+this machine or on a linked machine that has these levels, starts at **Off**.
+Threads that already exist keep their own choice, title and messages, so switch
+a fork you made earlier off separately.
+While a thread answers, its header shows **Answers linked questions**.
 
